<%= error_messages_for 'schedule' %>

<div class="box tabular">
  <%#
    THE TEMPLATE PICKER LISTS WHAT THIS ACTOR CAN SEE, and the controller re-resolves the
    id against the same scope. Two halves of one rule: a picker that offered more than the
    controller accepts would be a form that fails confusingly, and a controller that
    accepted more than the picker offers would be a disclosure hole reached through a
    hand-made request — somebody else's PRIVATE template, mailed to a list of your choosing.
  %>
  <p>
    <label for="schedule_template_id"><%= l(:field_redmine_reporter_dashboards_schedule_template) %>
      <span class="required">*</span></label>
    <%= select_tag 'schedule[template_id]',
                   options_from_collection_for_select(
                     RedmineReporterDashboards::Template.visible(User.current)
                                                        .where(project_id: @project.id)
                                                        .order(:name, :id),
                     :id, :name, @schedule.template_id
                   ),
                   include_blank: true %>
  </p>

  <p>
    <label for="schedule_query_id"><%= l(:field_redmine_reporter_dashboards_schedule_query) %></label>
    <%= select_tag 'schedule[query_id]',
                   options_from_collection_for_select(
                     IssueQuery.visible(User.current).where(project_id: [nil, @project.id])
                               .order(:name, :id),
                     :id, :name, @schedule.query_id
                   ),
                   include_blank: true %>
    <em class="info"><%= l(:text_reporter_schedule_query_info) %></em>
  </p>

  <p>
    <%= f.select :repeat,
                 RedmineReporterDashboards::Schedule::REPEATS.map { |r|
                   [l(:"label_reporter_schedule_repeat_#{r}"), r]
                 },
                 include_blank: true %>
  </p>

  <p><%= f.date_field :start_date, size: 10 %></p>
  <p>
    <%= f.date_field :end_date, size: 10 %>
    <em class="info"><%= l(:text_reporter_schedule_end_date_info) %></em>
  </p>

  <p>
    <%= f.text_field :email_subject, size: 60, maxlength: 255 %>
    <em class="info"><%= l(:text_reporter_schedule_subject_info) %></em>
  </p>

  <p>
    <%= f.text_field :timezone, size: 30, maxlength: 255 %>
    <em class="info"><%= l(:text_reporter_schedule_timezone_info) %></em>
  </p>

  <%#
    FR-45 AT THE POINT THE DECISION IS MADE. This is the field that decides whose numbers
    every recipient reads, so it says so here rather than only in the mail — an author
    choosing "a specific user" is choosing to send that person's view of the data to
    everybody on the list, and that is worth one sentence at the moment they pick it.
  %>
  <p>
    <%= f.select :render_as,
                 RedmineReporterDashboards::Schedule::RENDER_AS.map { |value|
                   [l(:"label_reporter_schedule_render_as_#{value}"), value]
                 } %>
  </p>
  <p>
    <%= f.select :render_as_user_id,
                 principals_options_for_select(@project.users.active.sorted,
                                               @schedule.render_as_user_id),
                 include_blank: true %>
    <em class="info"><%= l(:text_reporter_schedule_render_as_info) %></em>
  </p>

  <%#
    REDMINE USERS ONLY, AND ONLY THIS PROJECT'S. §7's row for the recipients table:
    "`user_id` only — no free-text to/cc/bcc/from, which is the exfiltration-and-
    spoofing-relay finding." There is no text field here because there is no column behind
    one; the controller additionally intersects the ids with this list, so a hand-made
    request cannot address somebody with no business in the project.
  %>
  <p>
    <label><%= l(:label_reporter_schedule_recipients) %></label>
    <%= select_tag 'schedule[recipient_user_ids][]',
                   options_from_collection_for_select(@project.users.active.sorted, :id,
                                                      :name, @schedule.recipients.map(&:user_id)),
                   multiple: true, size: 8, id: 'schedule_recipient_user_ids' %>
  </p>

  <p>
    <%= f.check_box :enabled %>
    <em class="info"><%= l(:text_reporter_schedule_enabled_info) %></em>
  </p>
</div>
